                <pb facs="0222" n="188" sameAs="frus:frus1870/pg188"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source"><hi rendition="#small-caps">No. 92.]</hi></note>
                <head>Mr. De Long to Mr.
                        Fish.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Legation
                                Yokohama,</hi><hi rendition="#italic"> Japan</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1870-10-10"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 10, 1870</date>. (Received November
                    25.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to inform you that on the
                    4th instant I received from the Japanese minister for foreign affairs a letter
                    (inclosure No. 1) inclosing to me a printed copy of the neutrality proclamation
                    issued by this government, (inclosure No. 2.) A copy of which I have duly
                    forwarded to the respective consular officers of our government in this
                    empire.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C. E. <hi rendition="#small-caps">De</hi> LONG.</signed></closer>



